{"id":"word:hebrew:H3201","type":"word","title":"יָכֹל","subtitle":"H3201 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to be able , literally ( can , could ) or morally ( may , might )","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to יָכֹל (H3201) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 194 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"יָכֹל (yâkôl) means to be able , literally ( can , could ) or morally ( may , might ) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 21 30."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"יָכֹל","transliteration":"yâkôl","pronunciation":"yaw-kole'","strong":"H3201","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3201","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["יוּכַ֣ל","אוּכַ֖ל","יוּכַ֥ל","אוּכַל֙","יוּכַ֖ל"],"morphs":[["HVqi3ms",39],["HVqi1cs",33],["HVqp3cp",31],["HVqi2ms",22],["HVqi3mp",15],["HVqp3ms",12],["HVqi1cp",11],["HVqi3fs",3],["HVqp1cs",3],["HC/Vqw2ms",3]]},"definitions":{"short":"to be able , literally ( can , could ) or morally ( may , might )","usage":"be able, any at all (ways), attain, can (away with, (-not)), could, endure, might, overcome, have power, prevail, still, suffer.","full":"H3201. yakol יָכוֺל יָכֹל, 193 verb be able, have power prevail, endure (Late Hebrew id. ; Aramaic יְכִיל ; Assyrian akâlu , Hpt in KAT 2Gloss i ,) — Qal Perfect יָכֹל Gen 32:26 8 t.; יָכוֺל 1Sam 4:15 2 t.; 3 feminine singular יָכְלָה Gen 36:7 ; Exod 2:3 ; 2 masculine singular וְיָכָלְתָּ֫ 18:23 ; 1 singular יָכֹלְתִּי Gen 30:8 2 t.; suffix יְכָלְתִּיו Psa 13:5 ; 3 plural יָכְ֑לוּ Gen 13:6 27t. + Josh 15:63 Qr; יָכֹ֑לוּ Exod 8:14 2 t.; Imperfect 3masculine singular יוּכָל Gen 13:16 34t.; יוּכָ֑ל Job 4:2 4 t.; וַיֻּכָ֑ל Hosea 12:5 ; 3 feminine singular תּוּכַל Amos 7:10 2 t.; 2 masculine singular תּוּכַל Gen 15:5 16 t.; 1 singular אוּכַל 19:19 30 t., etc. (on these Imperfect forms as irregular Qal, see Ges § 2 , R. 3 Kö i. 407 W SG 237 ; others Hoph`al ); Infinitive construct יְכֹ֫לֶת Num 14:16 ; Deut 9:28 ; Infinitive absolute יָכוֺל Num 13:20 ; 2Chr 32:13 ; יָכֹל Num 22:38 ; 1Sam 26:25 ; P 8 t. (not Leviticus), Ezekiel 3 t.; often J E D Jeremiah, Isa 2 , not seldom in Samuel Kings Chronicles; — 1 be able , to do a thing, whether ability be physical, moral, constitutional, or dependent on external authority; usually of man Gen 13:16 (J) +, but also of gods 2Chr 32:13 , 15 , and of ׳י Num 14:16 (JE), Deut 9:28 ; Jer 44:22 ; occasionally of inanimate things Amos 7:10 ; Gen 36:7 (P), Song 8:7 ; Eccl 1:15 (twice in verse), etc.: a. usually followed by infinitive with לְ (122 t.), Gen 31:35 I am not able to rise up ; 45:1 Joseph was not able to restrain himself , 45:3 ; 48:10 ; Exod 7:21 , 24 were not able to drink , 12:39 ; Josh 24:19 (all E); Gen 13:16 if a man can number the dust , 19:19 , 22 ; 43:32 ; 44:22 , 26 (twice in verse); Exod 10:5 ; 19:23 (all J), Gen 15:5 ; Exod 15:23 ; Num 11:14 (all J E) + 10 t. J E; Deut 7:17 10 t. D; Gen 13:6 they could not dwell together , 34:14 ; 36:7 ; Exod 9:11 ; 40:35 ; Num 9:6 ; Josh 9:19 (all P); 1Sam 3:2 ; 6:20 ; 1Kin 9:21 (on || 2Chr 8:8 and text of Judg 1:19 see Bu RS 8 ), Amos 7:10 ; Hosea 5:13 ; Zeph 1:18 ; Jer 6:10 ; 11:11 ; 13:23 ; 18:6 ; 19:11 +. b. followed by infinitive without לְ (27 t.; not P): Gen 37:4 ; Exod 2:3 ; 18:18 , 23 (all E), Gen 24:50 ; 44:1 (J), Num 22:37-38 , (JE), Deut 1:9 ; 7:22 ; 14:24 ; 22:29 ; Judg 8:3 ; Jer 49:10 , 23 ; Hab 1:13 ; Isa 46:2 ; 47:11-12 , 57:20 ; Lam 1:14 ; Psa 18:39 ; Psalm 36:13; 78:20 ; Prov 30:21 ; Job 4:2 ; 33:5 . c. with infinitive implicit, always negative, Gen 29:8 go and feed them; and they said, We are not able, cannot (J), Exod 8:14 (P), Isa 29:11 ; Jer 20:9 ; Psa 21:12 ; Jonah 1:13 . d. with negative = may not (of moral inability): Gen 43:32 (J) the Egyptians might not eat bread with the Hebrews; Judg 21:18 we may not give them wives; especially D, Deut 7:22 ; 12:17 ; 14:24 ; 16:5 ; 17:15 ; 22:3 ; 28:27 , 35 . e. be able , followed by imperfect: נַכֶּה אוּכַל אוּלַי Num 22:6 (JE) perchance I am able (so that) we smite (see Di; read perhaps נוּכַל for אוּכַל Ges § 120 , 1 b); יִגְּעוּ יוּכְלוּ לֹא Lam 4:14 they are unable, they touch = are unable to touch (Dr § 163 , Obs .) f. be able , followed by perfect consecutive, only very late, וְרָאִיתִי אוּכַל Est 8:6 (twice in verse), literally how shall I be able and see? — Also in various combinations where English idiom would make it an auxiliary to another verb: g. able to gain, accomplish: followed by acc נִקָּיוֺן יוּכְלוּ לֹא Hosea 8:5 how long will they be unable (to gain) innocence? תּוּכָ֑ל כִּיכֹֿל יָדַעְתִּ֯ Job 42:2 I know that thou art able (to do) all things ; דָּבָר אֶתְכֶם יוּכַל הַמֶּלֶךְ אֵין Jer 38:5 the king is not (one who is) able (to do) anything with ( אֶתְכם for אִתְּכֶם see Gf, i.e. against ) you. h. able to endure: וַעֲצָרָה אָוֶן אוּכַל לֹא Isa 1:13 I cannot endure iniquity and (with) a solemn assembly , Psa 101:5 . i. able to reach , followed by לְ , Psa 139:6 it is high, לָהּ אוּכַל לֹא I cannot (reach) to it. 2 prevail: a. absolute prevail, overcome, be victor Gen 30:8 (E), 32:29 (J), Hosea 12:5 ; 1Sam 26:25 ; 1Kin 22:22 2Chr 18:21 ; Jer 20:7 , 11 ; of waves 5:22 ; succeed Isa 16:12 ; Jer 3:5 (VB hast had they way ). b. followed by לְ person, prevail against, over Gen 32:26 (J), Num 13:30 (JE), Judg 16:5 ; 1Sam 17:9 ; Jer 1:19 ; 15:20 ; 20:10 ; 38:22 ; Obadiah 7; Psa 129:2 ; Est 6:13 . c. once with suffix, יְכָלְתִּיו Psa 13:5 I have prevailed over him , + Zech 9:15 (where read וְיָכְלוּם for וְאָֽכְלוּ with ᵑ7 ᵐ5 Klo ThLZ 1879. 564 Sta ZAW 1881, 18 ). 3 absolute have ability, strength , only negative אוּכָ֑ל לֹא מִשְּׂאֵתוֺ Job 31:23 because of his loftiness I have no ability , am inadequate (to anything).","rootNote":"or (fuller) יָכוֹל ; a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 21 30","keyReferences":["1Chr 21 30","1Kgs 3 9","1Kgs 5 17","1Kgs 8 11","1Kgs 9 21","1Kgs 